caption: Converting Marks to Character Points
rule: converting-marks-to-character-points

Each Drive Mark earns character points at the campaign's Mark Value in effect when that Mark is awarded.

Character points earned from a Mark = 1 × Mark Value at time of award

A common tested campaign value is 0.5 character points per Mark, or one character point per two Marks. This is an example rather than a universal GATES constant.

When conversion produces a fraction that cannot yet be spent, retain the underlying Mark record or fractional progress. Rounding never destroys earned progress.

Changing a source, changing a Secondary Choice, or later changing Mark Value does not retroactively recalculate previously earned character points.

Ad hoc awards, training points, Godmath, enhancement loops, and other advancement sources are tracked separately unless their own rules explicitly convert them into Drive Marks.
